    <h1>AI Tools for Beginners</h1>

    <p>
      Artificial intelligence tools can help people learn, research,
      write, organize ideas, create content, and complete many everyday
      tasks more efficiently.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 1 — Learn the Basics</h2>

    <p>
      Start by understanding what AI tools can and cannot do. Different
      tools are designed for different tasks.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 2 — Use AI for Learning</h2>

    <p>
      AI can help explain difficult topics, summarize information,
      generate practice questions, and help you organize your learning.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 3 — Use AI for Content Creation</h2>

    <p>
      AI can help you brainstorm ideas, create outlines, improve writing,
      and develop content concepts. Always review the result before
      publishing it.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 4 — Use AI to Improve Your Work</h2>

    <p>
      You can use AI to organize tasks, brainstorm solutions, analyze
      information, and automate parts of repetitive work where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 5 — Build a Useful Skill</h2>

    <p>
      Don't depend entirely on AI. Combine AI tools with a real skill,
      such as writing, design, marketing, coding, research, or customer
      support.
    </p>

    <h2>Important Tip</h2>

    <p>
      Always check important information yourself. AI can make mistakes,
      so verify facts before relying on them or sharing them with others.
    </p>

